• I found a likely root cause. math.Float64frombits is currently “inlined” by just returning its integer argument signal unchanged in call_inline.go:2322, which means dfsin can
  end up doing arithmetic on the raw uint64 bit pattern instead of on a float64 value. That matches the symptom exactly: zero works, then every nonzero case explodes into garbage.
  I’m checking the IR type machinery now so I can fix the intrinsic as an actual bit reinterpretation, not an untyped passthrough.

