• The deeper issue is confirmed: this compiler still treats native float64 values as plain 64-bit bitvectors, so +, *, /, unary -, and < on dfsin’s float64 locals are being
  emitted as integer operations. That means removing the fallback exposed a real missing lowering path, not just a missing intrinsic. I’m checking whether the existing CHStone
  soft-float helpers (float64_add, float64_mul, float64_div, comparisons, etc.) can be reused automatically for native float64 ops instead of trying to add true floating-point
  hardware semantics from scratch.

